1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,659
A one room hut.

2
00:00:01,659 --> 00:00:03,620
A big house with many rooms.

3
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:06,927
A college building with
labs, offices and a store.

4
00:00:07,327 --> 00:00:10,066
In the hut, everything
happens in one space.

5
00:00:10,066 --> 00:00:12,859
In the building, every
job has its own room.

6
00:00:13,309 --> 00:00:17,358
Aarav wondered: is a cell built
like the hut, or like the building?

7
00:00:17,358 --> 00:00:19,498
And does every cell have a nucleus?

8
00:00:19,848 --> 00:00:20,804
Two answers.

9
00:00:20,804 --> 00:00:22,785
Some cells are like the hut.

10
00:00:22,785 --> 00:00:26,421
They have no nuclear membrane,
and they are prokaryotic.

11
00:00:26,421 --> 00:00:29,910
Others are like the building,
with many walled rooms.

12
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:31,319
They are eukaryotic.

13
00:00:31,819 --> 00:00:36,519
By the end, you will know the parts of
a bacterium, the parts of a eukaryotic

14
00:00:36,519 --> 00:00:39,770
cell, and how to tell plant
and animal cells apart.

15
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:42,278
First, what do all cells share?

16
00:00:42,628 --> 00:00:47,107
Every cell has a cell membrane around
it, and a jelly inside, called the

17
00:00:47,107 --> 00:00:48,007
cytoplasm.

18
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:51,271
The cytoplasm is where most
of the cell's work happens.

19
00:00:51,721 --> 00:00:54,598
Every cell has ribosomes, tiny
bodies that make proteins.

20
00:00:54,598 --> 00:00:56,768
And every cell has genetic material, DNA.

21
00:00:57,418 --> 00:00:58,895
Let's zoom into the prokaryotes.

22
00:00:59,245 --> 00:01:03,593
Prokaryotes are bacteria, blue green
algae, mycoplasma and PPLO, which

23
00:01:03,593 --> 00:01:05,987
means pleuro pneumonia like organisms.

24
00:01:05,987 --> 00:01:10,648
Bacteria come in four basic shapes:
rod like bacillus, round coccus, comma

25
00:01:10,648 --> 00:01:12,896
shaped vibrio and spiral spirillum.

26
00:01:13,396 --> 00:01:15,036
Zoom into one bacterium.

27
00:01:15,036 --> 00:01:17,628
A cell wall surrounds the cell membrane.

28
00:01:17,628 --> 00:01:19,822
Only mycoplasma has no cell wall.

29
00:01:19,822 --> 00:01:23,851
Inside is the cytoplasm, with
ribosomes but no other organelles.

30
00:01:24,351 --> 00:01:25,251
Zoom again.

31
00:01:25,249 --> 00:01:29,721
There is no nuclear membrane, so
the DNA lies naked in the cytoplasm.

32
00:01:29,721 --> 00:01:34,095
Many bacteria also have small rings
of DNA outside the main DNA, called

33
00:01:34,095 --> 00:01:34,995
plasmids.

34
00:01:35,337 --> 00:01:39,968
Plasmids give bacteria special features,
like resistance to antibiotics.

35
00:01:39,968 --> 00:01:44,878
Prokaryotic cells are usually smaller,
and they multiply faster than eukaryotic

36
00:01:44,878 --> 00:01:45,778
cells.

37
00:01:46,157 --> 00:01:48,748
Now the eukaryotic cell, step by step.

38
00:01:49,098 --> 00:01:49,998
Step one.

39
00:01:49,617 --> 00:01:51,947
Eukaryotes are the protists,
plants, animals and fungi.

40
00:01:52,697 --> 00:01:53,597
Step two.

41
00:01:53,456 --> 00:01:57,632
Their cytoplasm is divided into many
rooms by membrane bound organelles.

42
00:01:57,632 --> 00:01:59,753
This is called compartmentalisation.

43
00:02:00,503 --> 00:02:01,403
Step three.

44
00:02:01,338 --> 00:02:05,485
They have a well organised nucleus,
with a nuclear envelope around it.

45
00:02:06,235 --> 00:02:07,135
Step four.

46
00:02:07,114 --> 00:02:10,467
Their genetic material is
organised into chromosomes.

47
00:02:11,217 --> 00:02:12,117
Step five.

48
00:02:11,987 --> 00:02:16,088
They have structures for moving and a
cytoskeleton, a frame of fibres that

49
00:02:16,088 --> 00:02:17,682
gives the cell its shape.

50
00:02:18,432 --> 00:02:19,641
Remember this.

51
00:02:19,641 --> 00:02:22,171
No nuclear membrane, prokaryotic.

52
00:02:22,171 --> 00:02:24,363
A true nucleus, eukaryotic.

53
00:02:24,963 --> 00:02:28,632
Now compare them side by
side, with one example each.

54
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:30,760
A bacterium is prokaryotic.

55
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:35,198
Its DNA is naked, it has no membrane
bound organelles, and it has only

56
00:02:35,198 --> 00:02:36,098
ribosomes.

57
00:02:36,431 --> 00:02:38,547
Your cheek cell is eukaryotic.

58
00:02:38,547 --> 00:02:43,688
Its DNA sits inside a nucleus, and it
has many organelles, like mitochondria,

59
00:02:43,688 --> 00:02:46,858
the endoplasmic reticulum
and the Golgi complex.

60
00:02:47,308 --> 00:02:51,583
In eukaryotic cells, ribosomes are
found in the cytoplasm, on the rough

61
00:02:51,583 --> 00:02:55,339
endoplasmic reticulum, and inside
chloroplasts and mitochondria.

62
00:02:55,989 --> 00:03:00,198
Eukaryotic cells come in two
big kinds, plant and animal.

63
00:03:00,548 --> 00:03:05,245
Plant cells have a cell wall,
plastids, and a large central vacuole.

64
00:03:05,245 --> 00:03:07,567
These are absent in animal cells.

65
00:03:08,017 --> 00:03:12,059
Animal cells have centrioles, which
are absent in almost all plant cells.

66
00:03:12,509 --> 00:03:16,904
Animal cells also have a centrosome,
which helps the cell divide.

67
00:03:17,554 --> 00:03:20,733
Let's list the organelles
a eukaryotic cell has.

68
00:03:21,083 --> 00:03:24,749
The endoplasmic reticulum, the Golgi
complex, lysosomes, mitochondria,

69
00:03:24,749 --> 00:03:26,139
microbodies and vacuoles.

70
00:03:26,589 --> 00:03:30,916
Each is wrapped in a membrane, so
each job gets its own room, just like

71
00:03:30,916 --> 00:03:32,279
the college building.

72
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:33,779
Your turn.

73
00:03:33,709 --> 00:03:37,691
A cell has a cell wall and
ribosomes, but no nuclear membrane.

74
00:03:37,691 --> 00:03:39,887
Is it prokaryotic, or eukaryotic?

75
00:03:39,887 --> 00:03:41,109
Pause and decide.

76
00:03:44,309 --> 00:03:45,209
Prokaryotic!

77
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:47,591
A missing nuclear membrane is the key.

78
00:03:47,591 --> 00:03:50,024
A cell wall alone does not decide it.

79
00:03:50,674 --> 00:03:52,304
Now, a worked example.

80
00:03:52,304 --> 00:03:53,838
Let's sort three cells.

81
00:03:54,188 --> 00:03:55,091
Cell one.

82
00:03:55,091 --> 00:03:56,037
Mycoplasma.

83
00:03:56,037 --> 00:03:59,946
It has no nuclear membrane,
and no cell wall either.

84
00:03:59,946 --> 00:04:01,411
It is prokaryotic.

85
00:04:01,861 --> 00:04:02,761
Cell two.

86
00:04:02,703 --> 00:04:04,553
A yeast cell, a fungus.

87
00:04:04,553 --> 00:04:06,824
It has a nucleus and organelles.

88
00:04:06,824 --> 00:04:08,140
It is eukaryotic.

89
00:04:08,590 --> 00:04:09,490
Cell three.

90
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,528
An onion cell.

91
00:04:10,528 --> 00:04:14,283
It has a nucleus, a cell wall
and a large central vacuole.

92
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:17,579
So it is eukaryotic,
and it is a plant cell.

93
00:04:18,229 --> 00:04:19,693
Now, the exam trap.

94
00:04:20,043 --> 00:04:23,410
Many students think prokaryotes have
no DNA, because they have no nucleus.

95
00:04:23,810 --> 00:04:25,456
But they do have DNA.

96
00:04:25,456 --> 00:04:29,951
It lies naked in the cytoplasm,
not wrapped in a nuclear membrane.

97
00:04:30,601 --> 00:04:32,085
Where is this asked?

98
00:04:32,085 --> 00:04:36,258
As statement questions comparing
prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells, and

99
00:04:36,258 --> 00:04:37,891
plant and animal cells.

100
00:04:38,491 --> 00:04:39,604
Exam level now.

101
00:04:39,604 --> 00:04:41,433
Which statements are correct?

102
00:04:41,433 --> 00:04:42,592
Pause and solve.

103
00:04:47,992 --> 00:04:50,553
The answer is B, statements one and three.

104
00:04:51,053 --> 00:04:52,602
Statement one is correct.

105
00:04:52,602 --> 00:04:55,104
Plasmids can give
resistance to antibiotics.

106
00:04:55,104 --> 00:04:56,973
Statement three is correct too.

107
00:04:56,973 --> 00:04:59,760
Centrioles are absent in
almost all plant cells.

108
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:01,780
Statement two is wrong.

109
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:03,588
Mycoplasma has no cell wall.

110
00:05:03,588 --> 00:05:05,155
Statement four is wrong.

111
00:05:05,155 --> 00:05:06,805
Prokaryotes have ribosomes.

112
00:05:07,405 --> 00:05:08,945
Here is your recap.

113
00:05:08,945 --> 00:05:10,528
Screenshot this card.

114
00:05:13,728 --> 00:05:15,914
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

115
00:05:16,314 --> 00:05:17,214
One.

116
00:05:16,749 --> 00:05:19,201
What are the four basic
shapes of bacteria?

117
00:05:20,101 --> 00:05:21,001
Two.

118
00:05:20,504 --> 00:05:21,602
What is a plasmid?

119
00:05:22,502 --> 00:05:23,402
Three.

120
00:05:23,029 --> 00:05:26,595
Name two things a plant cell has
that an animal cell does not.

121
00:05:27,695 --> 00:05:32,142
Next time: a bacterium has no bones
and no shell, so what keeps it from

122
00:05:32,142 --> 00:05:33,042
bursting?

123
00:05:32,861 --> 00:05:35,680
We find out in the
prokaryotic cell envelope.
